    "details": {
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p>Woodland guardians in perfect sync. Briar lords put the \"blade\" in blade of grass. As arbiters of the law of the forest, they judge the worthiness of all who enter the sacred spaces hidden deep within the woods. Those deemed unworthy face a final trial by combat.</p><p><strong>Vassals of Trees.</strong> Each briar lord serves under one or more treants, acting under their command to safeguard the forest from intrusion. Though not as powerful as the mighty shepherds of the forest, the lords' unflinching devotion has earned them the honour of defending the woods' most sacred sites.</p><p><strong>Blades of Grass.</strong> A briar lord in the forest is never unarmed—the verdant expanse offers itself freely as an armoury to its protectors. Simple branches twist themselves into razor sharp edges in a lord's grasp, while sap drawn from any tree grows toxic at their will.</p><p><strong>Lords' Council.</strong> In more vital locations, a single briar lord may prove insufficient—a council of three is thus formed to ensure the success of their sacred duties. By the time they reveal themselves to trespassers, a verdict has already been passed, and all that is left is to carry out the sentencing.</p><p><em>Habitat: Forest, Grassland, Jungle, Swamp; Treasure: Armament</em></p><p><em>Source: Heliana's Field Notes X-38 (Loot Tavern)</em></p>",
        "public": ""
      },
